s=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἵππῳ ἢ συνωρίδι ἢ ζεύγει</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">λαμπάδι</span></span>, etc.: c. acc. cogn. in same sense, <span class=\"gr\">πάντα ἐνίκα</span> he won all the bouts, , ; <span class=\"gr\">τὰ κοῦφα, τὰ μείζοναν.</span>, , ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τῶν παλαισμάτων ἓν ν.</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἅρμα ν.</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">παγκράτιον</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">ναυμαχίαν, μάχας,</span> , , etc.: freq. <span class=\"gr\">ν. Ὀλύμπια</span>to be conqueror in the Olympian games, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τὠλύμπια</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τὰ Παναθήναια</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ν. Ὀλυμπιάδα</span></span> (also <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ν. Ὀλυμπίασιν</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἐν Πυθίοισι</span></span>): c. dat. et acc., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τὰ Πύθια τῷ τεθρίππῳ ν.</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">πολλοὺς ἀγῶνας οὐ παγκρατίῳ μόνον, κτλ.,</span> ; <span class=\"gr\">Ὀλυμπίασι παῖδας στάδιον ν.</span>conquer in the boys' race in the stadium at Olympia, : c. dupl. acc., <span class=\"gr\">Πύθια ν. ἄνδρας</span> Diog.Cyn. ap. : also in <i>Att.</i> Inscrr. c. gen., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">Λεωντὶς ἀνδρῶν ἐνίκα</span></span>, al.: generally c. acc. cogn., <span class=\"gr\">νίκην ν.</span>win a victory, , , etc. (cf. infr. ); also <span class=\"gr\">ν. τρίποδα</span>win it, . </div><div>prevail, be superior,<span class=\"gr\">μύθοισιν, ἔγχεϊ,</span> ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">δόλοισι</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">κάλλει ἐνίκα</span> (sc. <span class=\"gr\">κρητήρ</span>) ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">πᾶσαν ἀρετὴν νενικηκώς</span></span>: c. <i>part.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">εὐεργετῶν ν.</span></span>. </div><div> of opinions, etc., <span class=\"gr\">βουλὴ κακὴ νίκησεν</span> the evil counsel prevailed, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τὰ χερείονα νικᾷ</span></span>, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἐνίκα ἡ γνώμη</span></span>, cf. , etc.; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἡ νικῶσα βουλή</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">ἐκ τῆς νικώσης [γνώμης]</span> according to the prevailing opinion, vote of the majority, , ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ταῦτ' ἐνίκα</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νικᾷ πάσαισι ταῖς ψήφοις ὁ νόμος</span>is carried,</span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">σὺν ψάφῳ τᾷ νικεούσᾳ</span></span> (Delph., iv B.C.): freq. of orators, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νικᾷ . . ὁ κακὸς ἐν πλήθει λέγων</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ν. γνώμῃσι</span></span> (so <span class=\"gr\">γνώμῃ,</span>v.l.<span class=\"gr\">γνώμην</span>, , cf.): freq. impers., <span class=\"gr\">ἐνίκα</span> (sc. <span class=\"gr\">ἡ γνώμη</span>) it was resolved, c. <i>inf.</i>, <span class=\"gr\">ἐνίκα μὴ ἐκλιπεῖν τὴν πόλιν</span>it was carried not . . , ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">τέλος γε μέντοι δεῦρ' ἐνίκησεν μολεῖν</span></span>, etc.; <span class=\"gr\">ἐνίκησε . . λοιμὸν εἰρῆσθαι</span>it was the prevailing opinion that . . , ; <span class=\"gr\">ἐν δημοκρατίᾳ νικᾷ ζῆν</span>it is preferable . . , . </div><div> c. <i>inf.</i>, succeed in . . , <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἐνίκησε σκορπίσαι</span></span>. </div><div> as law-term, <span class=\"gr\">ν. τὴν δίκην</span>win one's cause, , cf. ; simply <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νικᾶν</span></span> (Gortyn), , , (iii B.C.), etc.; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νικήσεις ἐν τῷ κρίνεσθαί σε</span></span>:—<i>Pass.</i>, c. gen., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">αἴ κα νικαθῇ τῶν ἐνεχύρων</span></span> (Crete, v B.C.); <i>v.</i> infr. . </div><div> c. acc., conquer, vanquish,<span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">Ἕκτορα</span></span>, etc.: freq. c. dat. modi, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">μάχῃ ν. Ἀχαιούς</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἀγορῇ ν. υἷας Ἀχαιῶν</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">πόδεσσι δὲ πάντας ἐνίκα</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">κάλλει ἐνίκων φῦλα γυναικῶν</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">πάντα ν. ἄνδρα . . κακοῖσιν</span>surpass him in miseries, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ν. τινὰ ἔν τινι</span></span>, etc.; <span class=\"gr\">μὴ φῦναι τὸν ἅπαντα νικᾷ λόγον</span>excels the whole account, (lyr.); <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίκα ἐν τῷ ἀγαθῷ τὸ κακόν</span></span>: c. acc. cogn., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">μάχην ν. τινά</span></span>, , etc.:—<i>Pass.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἔστιν ἃ τῶν ἄθλων δὶς ἕκαστος ἐνικήθη</span></span>: c. <i>part.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ν. ἀλεξόμενός τινα</span></span>, etc. </div><div> as law-term (cf. ), <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίκης τήν μιν ἐγὼ νίκησα</span></span>:—<i>Pass.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἧ δέ κα νικαθῇ</span></span>, al.; also of objects in dispute, damages, etc., recover, ib., al.:—<i>Pass.</i>, to be assigned, adjudicated, ib.. </div><div> generally, overpower, esp. of passions, etc., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νόον νίκησε νεοίη</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">μὴ φόβος σὲ νικάτω φρένας</span></span>, cf. ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">[φύσις] νικᾷ τῷ ἥσσονι τὸ μεῖζον τῆς ἐλπίδος</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">βαρεῖαν ἡδονὴν νικᾶτέ με</span> grievous is the pleasure ye win prevailing over me, : c. <i>inf.</i>, <span class=\"gr\">μηδ' ἡ βία σε . . νικησάτω τοσόνδε μισεῖν</span> let not violence prevail on thee to . . , : with gen. of comparison, <span class=\"gr\">νικᾷ γὰρ ἁρετή με τῆς ἔχθρας πολύ</span>weighs with me more than enmity, from the compar. force in <span class=\"gr\"