he goddess of victory, , cf. , etc.; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">Νίκη Ἀθάνα Πολιάς</span></span>, cf. (lyr.), . </div><div> Astrol., name of sixth <span class=\"gr\">κλῆρος,</span> , .</div></p>","inflection":"νίκ-η [i_] , ἡ","dict":"lsj"},"grc:name:Νίκη":{"id":"grc:name:Νίκη","lemma":"Νίκη","pos":"name","gloss":"Nike","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:verb:νικωμένη":{"id":"grc:verb:νικωμένη","lemma":"νικωμένη","pos":"verb","gloss":"feminine nominative/vocative singular of νῑκώμενος (nīkṓmenos)","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:noun:νίκην":{"id":"grc:noun:νίκην","lemma":"νίκην","pos":"noun","gloss":"accusative singular of νίκη (níkē)","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:name:Νίκην":{"id":"grc:name:Νίκην","lemma":"Νίκην","pos":"name","gloss":"accusative singular of Νῑ́κη (Nī́kē)","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:adj:νικηφόρος":{"id":"grc:adj:νικηφόρος","lemma":"νικηφόρος","pos":"adj","gloss":"bringing victory","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:name:Νικηφόρος":{"id":"grc:name:Νικηφόρος","lemma":"Νικηφόρος","pos":"name","gloss":"a proper name","src":"name"},"grc:verb:νίζω":{"id":"grc:verb:νίζω","lemma":"νίζω","pos":"verb","gloss":"wash the hands","src":"lsj","senses":["wash the hands","feet","to wash one's hands","from","purge, cleanse","wash off","he washed","off his","washing part","bathing","washing clothes","nigid","nig[uglide]"],"html":"<b>νίζω</b>, ; imper. <div class=\"sense\"><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζε</span></span>; <i>inf.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζειν</span></span>; <i>part.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζων</span></span>, : <i>Ep.</i><i>impf.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζον</span></span>, :— the <i>pres.</i><b>νίπτω</b>, analogically formed from <span class=\"gr\">νίψω ἔνιψα,</span> first in , cf. , , , , though uses <i>Med.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίπτομαι</span></span> (but <span class=\"gr\">δια-νιζέσθω</span> ib., <span class=\"gr\">περι-νιζέσθω</span> ib.): <i>fut.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψω</span></span>, : <i>aor.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἔνιψα</span></span>; <i>Ep.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψα</span></span>:—<i>Med.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζομαι</span></span> (v. supr.): <i>impf.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζετο</span></span>: <i>fut.</i><span class=\"gr\">νίψομαι</span> (v. <span class=\"gr\">ἀπο-, ἐκ-νίζω</span>), late <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νιφήσομαι</span></span>: <i>aor.</i><span class=\"gr\">ἐνιψάμην</span>; <i>Ep.</i><i>3</i><i>sg.</i><span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψατο</span></span>: <i>pf.</i><span class=\"gr\">νένιμμαι</span> (v. infr.): <i>aor.</i><i>Pass.</i><span class=\"gr\">ἐνίφθην </span>(<i>κατ</i>-) :—wash the hands or feet (v. sub fin.), <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίζε δ' ἄρ' ἆσσον ἰοῦσα ἄναχθ' ἑόν</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">αὐτὰρ ἐπεὶ νίψεν</span> ib., cf. ; <span class=\"gr\">τῷ σε πόδας νίψω</span> ib., cf. Orac. ap. ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἁ δὲ χεὶρ τὰν χεῖρα νίζει</span></span> l.c.:—<i>Med.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψατο δ' αὐτὸς χεῖρας</span></span>, cf. ; <span class=\"gr\">νίψασθαι,</span> abs., to wash one's hands, , etc.; <span class=\"gr\">χεῖρας νίψασθαι ἁλός</span> [with water] from the sea, (v. infr. ); <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψασθαι λίμνης πόδα</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">οὔρῳ νιψάμενος τοὺς ὀφθαλμούς</span></span>. </div><div> generally, purge, cleanse,<span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νίψαι καθαρμῷ</span></span>, cf. . </div><div>wash off,<span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἐπεί σφιν κῦμα θαλάσσης ἱδρῶ . . νίψεν ἀπὸ χρωτός</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἀπ' αὐτοῦ δ' αἷμα κελαινὸν νίζ' ὕδατι λιαρῷ</span></span>, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">φόνον ἐμῆς ἔνιψε χειρός</span></span>l.c.:—<i>Pass.</i>, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">αἷμα νένιπται</span></span>:—<i>Med.</i>, <span class=\"gr\">ἐκ ποταμοῦ χρόα νίζετο ἅλμην</span>he washed the brine off his skin [with water] from the river, .—Commonly used of washing part of the person, while <span class=\"gr\">λούομαι</span> is used of bathing,<span class=\"gr\">πλύνω</span> of washing clothes, etc.; but <span class=\"gr\">νίζω</span> is sts. used of things, <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">σπόγγοισι . . τραπέζας νίζον</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">[δέπας] ἔνιψ' ὕδατος καλῇσι ῥοῇσι</span></span>; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ὕδατι νίζειν . . πλίνθον</span></span>.—<i>Att.</i> Prose writers use the word only in compds., v.<span class=\"gr\">ἀπο-, ἐναπο-, ἐκ-νίζω.</span> (Cf. OIr. nigid, Skt. nénekti 'wash', niktá- 'washed', Gr. <span class=\"gr\">ἀ-νιπτό-ποδες, χέρνιβα,</span> I.- nig[uglide]-.)</div>","inflection":"νίζω, ; imper.","dict":"lsj"},"grc:name:Νῖσος":{"id":"grc:name:Νῖσος","lemma":"Νῖσος","pos":"name","gloss":"Nisos, Nisus","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:verb:νικῶν":{"id":"grc:verb:νικῶν","lemma":"νικῶν","pos":"verb","gloss":"present active participle of νικάω (nikáō)","src":"wiktionary","dict":"wiktionary"},"grc:noun:νιφάς":{"id":"grc:noun:νιφάς","lemma":"νιφάς","pos":"noun","gloss":"snowflake","src":"lsj","senses":["snowflake","snowstorm","snow","shower","storm","sleet"],"html":"<b>νιφ-άς</b>, <i>άδος</i>, <i>ἡ</i>, <div class=\"sense\">snowflake, (only in ), mostly in pl., <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ὥς τε νιφάδες χιόνος πίπτωσι θαμειαὶ ἤματι χειμερίῳ</span></span>; <span class=\"gr\">βρέχε . . χρυσέαις νιφάδεσσι,</span> a legendary statement of the wealth of Rhodes, ; <span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">ἔπεα νιφάδεσσιν ἐοικότα χειμερίῃσιν</span></span>, cf. : sg. in collect. sense, snowstorm,<span class=\"note\"><span class=\"gr\">νιφὰς ἠὲ χάλαζα</span></span>; <span class=